=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Coal County has come in under 90% of normal in January to February 37 of 75 years since 1951, more than any other pair. In 2025 that middle ran 181% of normal in April to May and 57% in November to December. So far in 2026 it shows 82% in January to February and 129% in March to April. Every one of the 8 grids had its driest year in 1963, as low as 45% of normal on grid 17234.</p>"}
